# Vercel builds the React app in web/ and publishes web/dist. Everything
# Python goes to Cloud Run via the Dockerfile instead.
#
#
# Note that excluding requirements.txt does NOT stop the CLI printing
# "Detected FastAPI" — detection reads the local directory before anything is
# uploaded, so .vercelignore cannot influence it. The settings in vercel.json
# take precedence regardless, which is why the answer to "Customize settings?"
# is always no.
#
# What is NOT excluded matters as much: web/src and web/package.json have to
# be uploaded, because Vercel runs the build. Only the build's inputs and
# outputs are dropped below.

app.py
mock_ee_backend.py
routes_catalog.py
catalog.py
series.py
ee_series.py
redaction.py
summary.py
geometry.py
cache.py
requirements.txt
requirements-dev.txt
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
pytest.ini

# The leading slashes are load-bearing. .vercelignore uses .gitignore syntax,
# where a bare `scripts/` matches a directory at ANY depth — so it also
# excluded web/scripts/, and web/scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.mjs never
# reached the builder. `prebuild` runs that script, so the build died with
# MODULE_NOT_FOUND before Vite started. Anchor anything meant to be root-only.
/bench/
/ingest/
/scripts/
/tests/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/

# Installed and built artefacts. Vercel runs `npm --prefix web ci` and the
# build itself, so uploading either is pure waste — and node_modules alone is
# ~244 MB, which is enough to kill the upload from Cloud Shell with a bare
# `Error: fetch failed` that names no cause.
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
.git/

# The prototype is kept in the repo for reference but is not deployed.
site-scanner.html

# demo/ is NOT excluded: vercel.json's buildCommand copies
# demo/site-scanner-demo.html into the build so it is served at /demo.

# Credentials. `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, so the same
# reasoning as .dockerignore applies: a real service account key is named
# <project>-<16 hex chars>.json and matches neither literal name below.
service-account-key.json
*.key.json
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.json
**/ee-backend/
.env
.env.*
